# The report-only vehicle. `A ⊑ ∃u.⊤` with `Range(u,G)`: the saturator lowers
# `∃u.⊤` to a deliberately SUBSUMER-LESS top witness (see
# `atomic_existential_rhs`: "the witness has no subsumers (⊤-equivalent), so it
# only ever triggers domain(R)"), so `Range(u)=G` is the one existential target
# that is NOT range-folded — and folding it would break the domain inference
# that witness exists for. `target_label` therefore returns `Err`, the witness
# has no IRI to key an injected `Q` on, and `build_model` reports
# `LabelNotClosed` while every WRITTEN axiom still holds.
#
# Chosen for DURABILITY. The fixtures this replaced (markerresidue.ofn and
# friends) were vehicles built on ENGINE DEFECTS, and issue #81's fix closed
# them, which broke five tests at once. This one is not a defect: it is a
# deliberate, documented under-approximation with a stated reason.
#
# Konclude agrees there is nothing non-trivial to derive here.
provenance: konclude-v0.7.0-1138
